      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Huggins emerged in the late 19th‑century Ozark frontier as a modest agrarian outpost, with homesteaders farming corn, wheat, and hay while raising hogs and cattle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
