      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/huggins_missouri",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the 1930s Great Depression, residents turned to gardening, hunting, and foraging, while New Deal programs helped restore soil and forests in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
